## EXPERIENCE

### **IT/Website Coordinator**

**Project Create** — Washington, DC | June 2023-Present

*Non-profit providing art education for youth in the city*

- Oversee Project Create digital infrastructure, including maintaining the [Project Create website](https://projectcreatedc.org), IT administration, software/hardware troubleshooting, and on-site event technical support.
- Build and refine web pages by turning visual concepts, designs, and provided assets into responsive, polished layouts that support programs, fundraising, and community engagement.
- Optimized website performance to achieve 5-10x faster loading speeds, significantly improving user experience.
- Implemented a digital asset management system to serve as a central repository for the organization's assets, streamlining access and reducing retrieval times, making collaboration easier and more efficient.
- Spearheaded NordPass password manager rollout, migrating organization credentials, performing platform administration, and training staff – strengthening organizational security and encouraging secure credential sharing.

### **Creative Director & Developer**

**N. Escobar Media** — Rockville, MD | November 2020-Present

*Small independent production studio*

- Founded [N. Escobar Media](https://nescobar.media), an independent production studio building innovative digital experiences and finding solutions to niche problems, using a wide variety of tools for both internal projects and external clients.
- Actively releasing projects, including: a number of JavaScript & TypeScript packages – like [modpack-lock](https://npmjs.com/package/modpack-lock) and [steploop](https://npmjs.com/package/steploop), games built in Godot and on hardware – like [Starfish](https://nickesc.itch.io/starfish) and [the BumbleBee](https://github.com/nickesc/bumblebee), other media projects and animations – like [The Poets Are Coming](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qajr-cAGY2Q), and more.
- Design and develop visually appealing, user-friendly websites for individuals and organizations, manage clients' digital workspaces, execute end-to-end domain management (DNS configuration, domain registration, Google Workspace integration and website deployment).
- Collaborate with clients to plan, design and build solutions to their needs, emphasizing clear communication with frequent updates, regular meetings and comprehensive plans outlining timelines, milestones and deliverables.

### **Program Assistant Coordinator**

**CCRC** — Waynesboro, PA | Summer 2021 and 2022

*Overnight summer camp and retreat center*

- Managed the Outdoor Adventure Program; supervised and trained 6-12 staff and multiple activity areas.
- Worked with staff and children of all ages and abilities in a fast-paced, chaotic environment while maintaining effective communication and leadership.
- Successfully planned and ran all campouts (8-10 per summer) and cookouts (1-2 per day) for all age groups.
- Facilitated 20+ retreat groups on the ropes course and zip lines, emphasizing safety and fun for all participants.

